---
name: design-research
description: Gather read-only design craft references and save project-relevant findings with provenance.
---

Read the brief and project rules, then verify the pinned manifest at session start. Research real reference work and techniques that address the actual audience and task. Record source, date, relevant detail, and how it informs or challenges the project's visual idea. Keep the Step 1 discovery ledger as well ([plan, Step 1](../../FANNAN-PLAN.md)): Maintain a discovery ledger for audience needs, current workflows, pain points and constraints. Record evidence source/date, assumptions, confidence, design consequence and risk. Use supplied or already-authorized research, support and analytics evidence. Assign material assumptions an owner and validation method in Step 5. Never present brief assertions or visual references as user research; preserve existing contact and payment approvals. Do not copy protected work or turn a reference into a default template. Before writing under `/workspace/design-output/<project>/`, run `"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh" "/workspace/design-output/<project>/" "<project>"`; see [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Remain read-only on external sites and the repo. Never post or buy access without Fadel's yes.

## Gotchas

- A reference helps the critic judge craft; it does not approve content facts or override the brief.
- A visual reference or a brief assertion is not user research; it never fills a discovery-ledger evidence field.
---
name: design-media
description: Prepare or generate project-approved images, edits, matching avatars, audio or short video through the selected connected media tool.
---

Read project settings/rules, asset brief, approved style references, permissions and intended placement. Verify the pinned manifest at session start; run `"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh" "/workspace/design-output/<project>/" "<project>"` before every local write. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Check price and ask Fadel **before anything that costs money, every time**. Never use GenerateImage or upload private screenshots, secrets or customer data to public links. Use only tools actually connected and supported; do not invent helper commands.

For matching avatars, read the project-owned avatar registry and reserve a distinct animal per bot; no two bots share an animal. A missing registry or duplicate assignment blocks generation and acceptance. Keep the registry in project files, not in this skill. Then derive a written style specification from the same approved references (framing, lighting, palette, edge treatment and expression range), then make a small private contact sheet after Fadel approves any cost. The shared-style rule is a review criterion: compare each result to the approved references side by side, record mismatches and reject inconsistent assets; it cannot be guaranteed by the generator. Record model/tool, source, license, consent, version and usage rights in the asset manifest. The project's writer supplies any embedded words; do not invent claims or names.

## Gotchas

- `/workspace/proto-bot/proto.py` has no documented media-search or resume command. Do not call either.
- An asset's technical availability is not usage permission; unresolved license or consent blocks handoff.
---
name: design-connect
description: Connect or repair only the design tool or related read-only service selected in project settings.
---

Read project settings and verify the pinned manifest at session start. Check the existing connection first; connect only what the user selected, one service at a time. Keep keys in the secret store and refer to variable names only. Fadel owns the existing Stitch key `STITCH_API_KEY`; rotate it every 90 days and immediately on suspected exposure. Resolve the reminder owner from project settings and record the due date. Never rotate or replace a live key without the existing authorization. For a project write, run `"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh" "/workspace/design-output/<project>/" "<project>"` first. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Do not post, spend, launch a build, alter a repo, or install software from this skill. If connection requires payment or a system change, present the exact action and await Fadel's yes in Fannan's chat.

## Gotchas

- Connection success does not prove a vendor operation can run; verify capability only when the task needs it.
