     8	At Steps 4–5 draw 1440px **grayscale structure only**; wait for the recorded Step 5 approval before color/type styling. At Step 6 trace the single visual idea to brief lines, use [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md), and name frames `<screen>/<state>/<version>`. Show default, hover, focus, disabled, empty, loading and error states. The seven baseline states are a minimum. Derive additional reachable states from actual interactions, including success/completion, selected/checked, expanded/collapsed, validation and read-only where applicable. Specify triggers, appearance, approved copy, semantics, announcements, keyboard/focus behavior and reference evidence. Success communicates the confirmed outcome and next action. The interaction critique fails when a reachable state or transition is unspecified. For every form, specify labels, required/optional indicators, accepted formats, help, validation timing, inline/summary errors, failure focus, input preservation and correction steps. Define submitting, success, failure, retry and duplicate-submission behavior. For consequential actions, specify cancellation, confirmation or undo as appropriate, plus unsaved-change behavior. Each applicable behavior requires approved interface copy and a task-level acceptance check; justify N/A. See the [handoff contract](../../references/handoff-contract.md). Also document language, direction, long-copy reflow and motion fallback. Preserve meaningful content and source-backed claims. In review mode, list evidence-backed copy, craft and WCAG 2.2 AA issues without altering source.
     9	
    10	## Gotchas
    11	
    12	- A vendor template or default palette never overrides the project's brief, approved wireframes or accessibility floor.
    13	- External sharing, generation with cost, or a design-system mutation needs Fadel's yes in Fannan's chat.
     1	---
     2	name: a11y-wcag-audit
     3	description: Audit a design prototype against WCAG 2.2 AA with automated and manual evidence for the engineer and QA gate.
     4	---
     5	
     6	Read the current project brief, settings, rules, languages and screen inventory. Verify the pinned manifest at session start; before saving results run `"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh" "/workspace/design-output/<project>/" "<project>"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). WCAG 2.2 AA is the minimum even if a project rule says less. Desktop stays first until its approval; a desktop audit does not approve mobile.
     7	
     8	Run available axe/Lighthouse and accessibility-tree checks on the rendered mock, then manually test keyboard traversal, focus visible and not obscured, focus order, target size, dragging alternatives, redundant entry, consistent help, errors, reduced motion/no-JS, page language and RTL/long-copy reflow. Record foreground/background contrast pairs, heading outline with one H1, standalone link/button names and intent for every image's alt text. For each issue record criterion, screen/state, element, evidence, severity, fix owner and retest result. Pass only with zero unresolved AA failures and complete manual evidence; unavailable checks are **untested** and block the Step 9 handoff. Give the project's engineer and QA gate actionable findings; do not edit source.
     9	
    10	## Gotchas
    11	
    12	- Automated zero violations does not cover focus behavior, language quality, meaningful labels or text clipping.
    13	- Color must never be the only signal for a state; record a second cue.
  for (const m of ['Text over images is graded in three zones on the faintest real glyph cluster', '(b) clearly below 3:1 (5% under it) FAILS, and no review can override it', 'AND names the worst region checked in `worstRegion`', 'A text-shadow or halo counts as the text\'s background', 'a caption at 70% opacity is measured, not refused', 'Letter clusters are never dropped on a background that is not solid', 'at most a quarter of the font size in both directions', 'The fallback content inside `video`, `audio`, `object` and `canvas` is not rendered either', 'text matches only text, so a heading with the same words never stands in for a lost button', 'a prefix or abbreviation of its 1440 name', 'one declared state shows ALL the clamped content at that width', 'a control inside a clamp is never excused', 'no unrecoverable clipping or truncation (read-more clamps follow the declared-state rule above)']) assert.ok(quality.includes(m), `design-quality.md: ${m}`);
