| R23-GPT-03 | A | P2 | [width-screen.mjs:45](/workspace/panel-r23/fannan/release/tools/width-screen.mjs:45), [width-screen.mjs:117](/workspace/panel-r23/fannan/release/tools/width-screen.mjs:117) | **Named-control boxes replace rendered text geometry.** `contentRects` returns `[el.getBoundingClientRect()]` for a control. Concrete page: at 320, a 100 px inline-block link contains a 240 px nowrap label inside a 100 px `overflow:hidden` wrapper. Executed identical-geometry DOM probes: **d9e1049 records the partial text clip; eeeb371 records no clip**, calls the wrapper a media crop and reports the link as shown. This regresses the rendered-range requirement established in **N02**. Browser rendering **UNVERIFIED**. | Measure the control box **and** its rendered text ranges. Keep media-only crops exempt, but never substitute the control box for its label’s geometry. Add a browser regression with direct link text overflowing its box, plus a fitting-label positive case. |
